<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 17 December, from 546 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/totila" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/totila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">546 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,480 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Totila's Ostrogoths take Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a long siege, the Ostrogothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/totila">Totila</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> when Isaurian guards opened a gate. The city, fought over repeatedly in Justinian's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic War</a>, was left largely depopulated.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">920 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Romanos I Lekapenos is crowned co-emperor with Constantine VII</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-i-lekapenos">Romanos I Lekapenos</a>, an admiral of humble origin and father-in-law of the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a>, was crowned co-emperor and governed in his place. He made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> in 927 and ruled until his sons deposed him in 944.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-i-lekapenos">Romanos I Lekapenos</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/942">942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,084 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Longsword of Normandy is murdered at Picquigny</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-longsword">William Longsword</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rollo">Rollo</a> and ruler of Normandy since about 927, was ambushed and killed by men of Arnulf I, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, at a peace conference at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picquigny">Picquigny</a>. He left his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> as heir.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-longsword">William Longsword</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1297">1297 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">729 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Myinsaing brothers overthrow King Kyawswa of Pagan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyawswa-of-pagan">Kyawswa of Pagan</a>, who held little more than the capital and had accepted Yuan overlordship to protect himself, was overthrown by the three Myinsaing brothers, nominally his viceroys. It marked the de facto end of the Pagan Kingdom.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyawswa-of-pagan">Kyawswa of Pagan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1538">1538 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">488 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Paul III excommunicates Henry VIII</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-iii">Pope Paul III</a> published the bull of excommunication against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>, prepared in 1535 but suspended. It came after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s agents destroyed the shrine of Thomas Becket at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1903">1903 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">123 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Wright brothers make the first powered flights</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Kill Devil Hills near Kitty Hawk, North Carolina, Orville Wright flew the Wright Flyer for 12 seconds and about 37 metres. Of four flights that day, Wilbur's longest lasted 59 seconds.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Graf Spee is scuttled off Montevideo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Believing a superior British force waited outside, Captain Hans Langsdorff scuttled the Admiral Graf Spee in the River Plate. He took his own life three days later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Simpsons premieres as a series</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fox broadcast the first full episode of The Simpsons, a Christmas special. It became the longest-running American animated series and scripted primetime show.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 17 December <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ernest-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ernest-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ernest of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1554–1612</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abdul-rahim-khan-i-khanan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abdul-rahim-khan-i-khanan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abdul Rahim Khan-i-Khanan</span><span class="tp">1556–1627</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/prince-rupert-of-the-rhine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prince-rupert-of-the-rhine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Prince Rupert of the Rhine</span><span class="tp">1619–1682</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kazys-grinius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kazys-grinius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kazys Grinius</span><span class="tp">1866–1950</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-francis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-francis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Francis</span><span class="tp">1936–2025</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 17 December <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sturmi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sturmi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sturmi</span><span class="tp">c. 705–779</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-longsword"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-longsword.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Longsword</span><span class="tp">c. 893–942</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-v-count-of-hainaut"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/baldwin-v-count-of-hainaut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Baldwin V, Count of Hainaut</span><span class="tp">1150–1195</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rumi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rumi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rumi</span><span class="tp">1207–1273</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/simon-bolivar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Simón Bolívar</span><span class="tp">1783–1830</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marie-louise-duchess-of-parma"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marie-louise-duchess-of-parma.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marie Louise, Duchess of Parma</span><span class="tp">1791–1847</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-gomes-da-costa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-gomes-da-costa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel Gomes da Costa</span><span class="tp">1863–1929</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thubten-gyatso"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thubten-gyatso.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thubten Gyatso</span><span class="tp">1876–1933</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
